JavaScript (JavaScript Language) is a programming language that allows developers to add interactivity and dynamic behavior to web pages. It runs on the client-side of the web browser and interacts with the server-side code running on the server. JavaScript can be used to manipulate the appearance of a webpage, such as changing colors or adding images, as well as perform calculations or interact with user input.

