Distance between sun and earth = 1059 km / 365 days

This gives us approximately 2.8 km as the distance between the sun and Earth during an eclipse. To calculate how long the eclipse lasts, we need to divide the total distance traveled by the distance between the sun and Earth during an eclipse:

Time for eclipse = Total distance / Distance between sun and earth

