However, if there is no clear sky above you, you may only see the faint outline of the moon, known as a partial lunar eclipse. In this case, the moon will still cast a shadow on the ground, but the light from the sun will be blocked by the Earth's atmosphere, making the moon appear dimmer than when it is fully illuminated.

